{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>She shall remain.</b> תֵּשֵׁב is nothing but a term of tarrying, as in ״וַתֵּשְׁבוּ בְקָדֵשׁ״ (Deuteronomy 1), ״וַיֵּשֶׁב בְּאֵלֹנֵי מַמְרֵא״ (Genesis 13)." "<b>In the blood of purification.</b> Even though she is seen [to be] clean." "<b>In the blood of purification.</b> The heh is not vocalized with a vowel, and it is a noun like טֹהַר." "<b>Days of purification.</b> The heh is vocalized — the days of her purification." "<b>In any sacred thing.</b> To include terumah, for this one is a long tevul yom — she immersed at the end of seven [days], and her intercourse does not bring her to purification until sunset of the fortieth day, [after] which on the next day she brings the atonement of her purification." "<b>She shall not touch.</b> A warning to one who eats, etc. — as is taught in Yevamot (75a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:07.660326126Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}